; Merge this section into Data\SKSE\Plugins\higgs_vr.ini.
; Case-insensitive registered client names. Higher priority wins.
; Routed candidates use the assigned executor PROVIDER's priority.
; An action-specific provider/decimalActionId entry overrides the provider default.
; The HIGGS native grab candidate (eligible grip or trigger) uses HIGGS/1 when its target is currently eligible.
; Equal priorities use provider, action, optional stable target and recognizer.
; Offers with identical keys and different targets need a stable target key.
; Empty Priorities clears overrides. Invalid/duplicate/overflow values preserve
; the previous complete map and log a warning. Up to 64 entries / 8190 characters.
[HandBroker]
Priorities=BodySlots=20,HIGGS/1=25,ExampleClimbing=50,ExamplePouchProvider=30
